CALLHOME German (diarization — DER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Gold speaker segments for the `callhome-de` dataset derive from CALLHOME German
(TalkBank / `talkbank/callhome`, config `deu`).

  TalkBank is free to use under its cite-to-use terms (no redistribution of the
  underlying LDC audio). Citation:
    MacWhinney, B. (2007). The TalkBank Project. TalkBank.
    CALLHOME German, LDC.
  Source:
    https://ca.talkbank.org/  ·  https://huggingface.co/datasets/talkbank/callhome

Per TalkBank's terms we do NOT redistribute CALLHOME audio; the loader
materialises it locally from the HF dataset the reproducer downloads. Only derived
RTTM label text would be a Tier-1 commit candidate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If a future dataset forbids redistributing its reference transcripts, do NOT
commit them: commit only the hypothesis + a reference hash/id, and let
`scripts/verify.py` pull the references from Hugging Face at re-score time.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Normalization provenance (flozi normalize_text)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The flozi-canonical text normalization in `raven_eval_core/flozi_wer.py`
(`normalize_flozi`) is ported from the `normalize_text` function published on
the `flozi00/asr-german-mixed-evals` HuggingFace dataset card. Credit to
Florian Zimmermeister (flozi00). The upstream dataset card declares no explicit
license for that snippet; it is ~25 lines of mechanical string transforms
(regex/transliteration/number-word handling) and is credited here in good faith.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party runtime dependencies / licenses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The package code is MIT (see LICENSE). Reproducing the *published WER numbers*,
however, hard-depends on two copyleft libraries on the scoring code path, and
they cannot be swapped for permissively-licensed alternatives without changing
the numbers:

  - unidecode   — GPL-2.0-or-later. Used for the flozi transliteration step.
  - num2words   — LGPL. Pulled in on the diagnostic-normalization path.
    (`text2num`/`alpha2digit` provides the flozi words→digits direction.)

Distributing raven.eval as source keeps the MIT-licensed code MIT — you install
these deps yourself from PyPI under their own terms. But anyone who ships a
*bundled* wheel, container image, or other combined/derived distribution that
includes these libraries inherits their GPL/LGPL copyleft obligations. Bundle
accordingly.
